# OneMira MCP & Mira CLI Best Practices

OneMira connects spoken meeting context captured on the standalone OneMira C1 recorder (and transcribed locally in OneMira Desktop on a supported macOS or Windows computer) into Cursor via the official Model Context Protocol server (`io.github.onemira-space/onemira-mcp`) and the `mira` CLI.

## Cursor MCP Configuration (`.cursor/mcp.json`)

- Prefer `npx -y @onemira-space/onemira-mcp` in `.cursor/mcp.json` so Cursor agents can query local transcripts, speaker labels, and OKF Markdown Wiki notes without cloud uploads.
- Never hardcode personal vault paths in committed repository files; rely on OneMira Desktop local discovery or environment variables.

```json
{
  "mcpServers": {
    "onemira": {
      "command": "npx",
      "args": ["-y", "@onemira-space/onemira-mcp"]
    }
  }
}
```

## Querying Spoken Context Before Implementation

- Search recent decisions and requirements first with `mira_search` or `mira_sessions` (`action: "list"`) before reading full raw segments.
- Retrieve exact verbatim quotes and speaker attribution (`Speaker ID`) with `mira_segments` on the relevant session ID rather than guessing spoken requirements.
- Read structured topic and project pages via `mira_wiki_read` / `mira_wiki_search` (Google Native OKF Markdown with YAML frontmatter and deterministic links).
- Keep generated action items, ADR summaries, and Wiki updates concise, deterministic, and grounded strictly in verified transcript segments.
